            {
              "text": "In Brisbane’s prestige real estate market (typically properties starting north of $3 million and extending into eight-figure riverfront estates), a substantial portion of transactions occur **off-market or pre-market**. Securing top-tier assets in blue-chip enclaves—such as New Farm, Teneriffe, Ascot, Hamilton, Hawthorne, Bulimba, and Paddington—requires established agent relationships, discretion, and technical due diligence.\n\nThe leading luxury buyers' advocates and acquisition advisory firms operating in Brisbane specialize in prestige residential property:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Cohen Handler Queensland\n* **Key Figures:** Jordan Navybox, James Navybox\n* **Prestige Focus:** Ultra-luxury, trophy riverfront homes, and high-stakes off-market acquisitions.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Cohen Handler is one of the highest-volume buyer’s agencies in Australia, and its Queensland arm has become a dominant force in Brisbane’s upper echelon. They have brokered some of the city's highest-profile off-market sales, including the landmark $25 million riverfront parcel at Julius Street, New Farm, and $23 million at Sutherland Avenue, Ascot. They are especially suited for high-net-worth individuals (HNWIs) seeking aggressive sourcing and direct access to unlisted trophy estates.\n\n### 2. Property Pursuit\n* **Key Figures:** Meighan Wells (formerly Hetherington)\n* **Prestige Focus:** Executive family residences, architectural homes, and expat repatriation.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Founded in 2003, Property Pursuit is one of Brisbane’s longest-running dedicated buyer's agencies. They have a reputation for methodical, discreet acquisition advisory, working heavily with medical executives, corporate leaders, and returning expatriates. Their advisory model focuses heavily on forensic property evaluation, street-by-street micro-location analysis, and long-term capital preservation.\n\n### 3. Streamline Property Buyers\n* **Key Figures:** Melinda Jennison, Scott Jennison\n* **Prestige Focus:** High-value character homes, riverfront assets, and comprehensive acquisition advisory.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Melinda Jennison (a multi-time REIQ Buyer's Agent of the Year and former REBAA President) and Scott Jennison (builder/project background) offer a technical, data-driven approach to high-end buying. For prestige buyers interested in heritage Queenslanders, renovations, or complex architectural parcels, their deep understanding of zoning, building costs, and risk management is invaluable.\n\n### 4. Wendy Russell Independent Buyers Advocate\n* **Key Figures:** Wendy Russell\n* **Prestige Focus:** Bespoke private client representation, high-stakes negotiations, and architectural homes.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Wendy Russell operates a high-touch, boutique advisory model that deliberately caps client intake to provide personal, partner-level attention. She is regarded for sharp negotiation tactics, deep emotional detachment in bidding, and strictly independent advisory without volume-driven incentives.\n\n### 5. PMC Property Buyers (Brisbane Office)\n* **Key Figures:** Will Tremain, Dimitri Stephanos\n* **Prestige Focus:** Blue-chip inner-ring acquisitions and luxury investment advisory.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Several of PMC’s key advisors have backgrounds as certified practicing property valuers (CPVs). This gives them a distinct analytical edge when pricing unique, one-of-a-kind prestige homes where traditional comparable sales data is sparse or distorted by off-market dynamics.\n\n### 6. Joanna Boyd Buyers Advocate\n* **Key Figures:** Joanna Boyd\n* **Prestige Focus:** Luxury family estates, lifestyle properties, and interstate/overseas relocations.\n* **Why They Stand Out:** Joanna Boyd provides tailored, end-to-end relocation and acquisition services for affluent families targeting top school catchments and prestige inner-city pockets (Ascot, Clayfield, Chelmer, Graceville, Paddington).\n\n---\n\n### What to Prioritize When Selecting a Prestige Advocate in Brisbane\n\n1. **Access to Elite Selling Networks:** Ensure the advocate has direct channels to Brisbane’s key prestige sales agents (e.g., Place Estate Agents, Ray White New Farm, Sotheby’s International Realty). A large percentage of prime Brisbane real estate trades without ever reaching online portals.\n2. **Brisbane-Specific Due Diligence:** The Brisbane luxury market features unique physical risks:\n   * **Flood and overland flow modeling** for riverfront properties (Bulimba, New Farm, St Lucia, Fig Tree Pocket, Chelmer).\n   * **Brisbane City Council Traditional Building Character (TBC) overlays**, which dictate what can and cannot be altered on pre-1946 character homes.\n   * **Topography and geotechnical stability** on steep prestige ridges in areas like Hamilton Hill or Paddington.\n3. **True Independence (REBAA Membership):** Ensure the agency acts exclusively for buyers, receives zero referral commissions from developers or selling agents, and avoids internal dual-agency conflicts.",
